 "knowledge": "",
 "markdown": "## Summary\nChange the dashboard's visible page title from \"Customer Dashboard\" to \"My Dashboard\".\n\n## How it works today\nThe page uses the `oj-sp-general-overview-page` template, whose `page-title` attribute is set to \"Customer Dashboard\" in the HTML. The template renders this as the page header title.\n\n## What changes\nOnly the `page-title` attribute value changes; everything else stays the same.\n\n## The change\n- `customer-dashboard-page.html` — change the `page-title` attribute from \"Customer Dashboard\" to \"My Dashboard\".\n\n## After the change\nWhen the person opens the Customer Dashboard page, the header at the top will read \"My Dashboard\" instead of \"Customer Dashboard\". The subtitle, tiles, table and all actions are unchanged.\n\n## Risks\nNone known. The title is display-only text on this single page and is not referenced by any chain, variable or navigation.\n\n## How to test\n1. Open the app and navigate to the customer dashboard (/vp/shell/customer-portal/customer-dashboard).\n2. Confirm the page header now reads \"My Dashboard\".\n3. Confirm the subtitle, KPI tiles, Recent Activity table and the New Request / Browse Catalog actions all still appear and work.\n\n## Questions\nNone.",
